<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cockburn Town</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cockburn Town is the capital of the Turks and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caicos-islands">Caicos Islands</a>, on the island of Grand Turk. It grew from the settlement of Bermudian salt rakers who worked the salt ponds of Grand Turk from the late 17th century, and salt remained the islands' chief export for two centuries. Its streets preserve buildings of the Bermudian colonial style, and it has remained the seat of government although <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/providenciales">Providenciales</a> has become the economic centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cockburn-town.jpg" alt="Cockburn Town" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original uploader was Seanjacksontc at en.wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cockburn_Town.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
